---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PUBLISHER } from '../consts';
const updated = '2026-08-12';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy"
      description="How App-Tipps.com collects, uses and protects personal data, your rights under UK GDPR and EU GDPR, and how to exercise them.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose" style="padding:34px 0 10px">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated 12 August 2026. This policy replaces all earlier versions.</p>

      <h2>Who is responsible for your data</h2>
      <p>
        App-Tipps.com is operated by {PUBLISHER.legalName} ("we", "us"), a company registered in England
        and Wales under number {PUBLISHER.companyNumber}, with its registered office at {PUBLISHER.address.street},
        {' '}{PUBLISHER.address.city} {PUBLISHER.address.postcode}, {PUBLISHER.address.country}. We are the data
        controller for personal data collected through this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        For any privacy question or request, contact <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect, and why</h2>
      <h3>Information you give us</h3>
      <p>
        If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you put in the message. We use it
        only to handle your enquiry. Legal basis: legitimate interests (responding to correspondence).
        We keep enquiry email for 24 months.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you subscribe to our newsletter, we store the name and email address you provide and the
        topics you selected. Legal basis: your consent. You can withdraw it at any time using the
        unsubscribe link in any newsletter, or by emailing us. We delete unsubscribed records within 30 days.
      </p>
      <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting and security provider, Cloudflare, processes your IP address and basic request data
        to deliver pages and to protect the site from attack. This is necessary to run the site securely.
        Legal basis: legitimate interests (security and service delivery). These logs are short-lived
        and we do not use them to identify individuals.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not require accounts, we do not host comments, and we do not ask for payment details.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site is funded by advertising. Advertising and measurement technologies that are not
        strictly necessary only run if you consent to them. Where consent is required, we ask for it
        through a consent management platform that is certified by Google and integrated with the IAB
        Europe Transparency and Consent Framework, as Google requires for publishers serving ads to
        users in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland.
      </p>
      <p>
        Depending on your choices, the following may process data about your visit:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> (as an advertising provider) may set or read identifiers to serve ads,
          limit how often you see the same ad, and measure performance. If you consent to personalised
          advertising, Google and its advertising partners may build a profile of your interests. See
          {' '}<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses data on sites that use its services</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong>, if enabled, tells us which pages are read and how people arrive.
          IP addresses are anonymised and we do not use analytics data to identify individuals.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Affiliate partners</strong> may set a cookie when you click an affiliate link, so the
          merchant can attribute a sale to us. This happens on the merchant's site, under the merchant's
          own privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can change or withdraw your choices at any time from the consent settings link in the site
        footer. Full detail of each cookie category is in our <a href="/cookie-policy/">Cookie Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal data. We share it only with processors and partners that help us run the
        site: our hosting and CDN provider, our email and newsletter provider, our consent management
        provider, and our advertising and analytics providers where you have consented. We may also
        disclose data where the law requires it, or to establish or defend legal claims.
      </p>

      <h2>International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Some of these providers are based outside the UK and EEA, including in the United States. Where
        data is transferred, it is protected by an adequacy decision, by Standard Contractual Clauses,
        or by an equivalent safeguard required under UK GDPR and EU GDPR.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>If you are in the UK, EEA or Switzerland, you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>access the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>have inaccurate data corrected;</li>
        <li>have your data deleted;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how we process it, including objecting to direct marketing at any time;</li>
        <li>receive your data in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw consent at any time, without affecting processing that already happened.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}`}>{PUBLISHER.privacyEmail}</a> with "Data request"
        in the subject line. We respond within one month. If you are unhappy with our response, you can
        complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office at
        {' '}<a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, or to your
        national supervisory authority in the EEA.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is written for a general adult audience and we do not knowingly collect personal data
        from children under 16. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, contact us and
        we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We update this policy when our practices change. The date at the top always shows the current
        version. Material changes will be announced on this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
